            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p01",
          "marks": 2,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p01_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Identifies the 16 equally likely sample space pairs $(d_1, d_2)$ and counts outcomes for each absolute difference."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p01_c2",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Confirms correct counts: 4 pairs for diff 0, 6 pairs for diff 1, 4 pairs for diff 2, 2 pairs for diff 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p02",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p02_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Calculates $E(X) = 0\\left(\\frac{4}{16}\\right) + 1\\left(\\frac{6}{16}\\right) + 2\\left(\\frac{4}{16}\\right) + 3\\left(\\frac{2}{16}\\right) = \\frac{20}{16} = 1.25$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p02_c2",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Calculates $E(X^2) = 0^2\\left(\\frac{4}{16}\\right) + 1^2\\left(\\frac{6}{16}\\right) + 2^2\\left(\\frac{4}{16}\\right) + 3^2\\left(\\frac{2}{16}\\right) = \\frac{0 + 6 + 16 + 18}{16} = \\frac{40}{16} = 2.5$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p02_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Obtains exact variance $\\text{Var}(X) = 2.5 - (1.25)^2 = 2.5 - 1.5625 = 0.9375 = \\frac{15}{16}$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p03",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p03_c1",
              "type": "B1",
              "text": "Finds standard deviation $\\sigma = \\sqrt{0.9375} = \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4} \\approx 0.968$ (to 3 s.f.)."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p03_c2",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Identifies the interval $(1.25 - 0.968, 1.25 + 0.968) = (0.282, 2.218)$, which includes the integer values $X = 1$ and $X = 2$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq06_p03_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Calculates $P(X \\in \\{1, 2\\}) = P(X = 1) + P(X = 2) = \\frac{6}{16} + \\frac{4}{16} = \\frac{10}{16} = \\frac{5}{8} = 0.625$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq07",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq07_p01",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq07_p01_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Identifies total number of ways to choose 3 components from 10 as $\\binom{10}{3} = 120$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq07_p01_c2",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Calculates $P(X = 0) = \\frac{\\binom{7}{3}}{120} = \\frac{35}{120}$ and $P(X = 1) = \\frac{\\binom{3}{1}\\binom{7}{2}}{120} = \\frac{3 \\times 21}{120} = \\frac{63}{120}$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq07_p01_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Calculates $P(X = 2) = \\frac{\\binom{3}{2}\\binom{7}{1}}{120} = \\frac{3 \\times 7}{120} = \\frac{21}{120}$ and $P(X = 3) = \\frac{\\binom{3}{3}}{120} = \\frac{1}{120}$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq07_p02",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq07_p02_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Calculates expectation $E(X) = \\frac{0(35) + 1(63) + 2(21) + 3(1)}{120} = \\frac{108}{120} = 0.9$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_discrete_random_variables_m02_l02_cpq07_p02_c2",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Calculates $E(X^2) = \\frac{0(35) + 1(63) + 4(21) + 9(1)}{120} = \\frac{156}{120} = 1.3$ and obtains $\\text{Var}(X) = 1.3 - (0.9)^2 = 1.3 - 0.81 = 0.49$."
            },
            {
